Special Keys
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

The following are a list of special keys and their associated functions:

   Execution Functions
        @118[<F4>]        Run
        @116[<F10>]       Step
        @117[<Shift F10>] Step 'n' Times
        @168[<F9>]        Set/Clear Breakpoint
        @169[<Shift-F9>]  Set/Clear Multi-Breakpoint

   Memory Functions
        @60[<Ctrl-D>] Dump Memory
        @62[<Ctrl-F>] Fill Memory
        @63[<Ctrl-G>] Go To Memory
        @61[<Ctrl-M>] Load Memory
 
   Window Sizing Functions
         @14[<Shift-F5>] Grow Window Vertically
         @15[<Shift-F6>] Shrink Window Vertically
         @16[<Shift-F7>] Grow Window Horizontally
         @17[<Shift-F8>] Shrink Window Horizontally

   Window Movement Functions
         @9[<F5>] Move Window Up
         @10[<F6>] Move Window Down
         @11[<F7>] Move Window Left
         @12[<F8>] Move Window Right

   Window Selection Functions
        @4[<ESC>]    Close Current Window
        @5[<F2>]     Go To Next Window
        @1[<F3>]     Go To Menu Bar
        @8[<Ctrl-L>] List/Go To Specific Window

   Window Display Functions
        @175[<F1>]     Help
        @18[<Ctrl-T>] Toggles Window Display Format

.178
General Info
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This program performs a software simulation of the Analog Devices ADSP-2100 
family Point Digital Signal Processor.  

This program is controlled by a menu driven, graphical user interface.  Items
are selected and controlled from the keyboard and/or mouse.  A menu bar at the
top of the screen provides access to windows and functions.  In addition, some
functions can be invoked directly from the keyboard whenever a special key is
pressed.  

An online help system provides help at any time simply by pressing the <F1> key
or by selecting the Help option from the menu bar.  

Further information available:

                        - @175[Help on Help System]
                        - @1[Menu Bar]
                        - @177[Special Keys]
                        - @176[Index]
               
.179
File Menu Option
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This submenu controls file related functions of the simulator.  Choices within
this submenu are:

   @95[Load Executable File]      - Loads an executable file into the simulator
   @97[Load Window File]          - Loads a window file into the simulator
   @98[Save Window File]          - Saves current configuration into a file
   @102[Display File]              - Displays a text file
   @101[Playback Keystroke File]   - Replays a keystroke file
   @99[Start Keystroke Recording] - Records keystrokes to a file
   @100[Stop Keystroke Recording]  - Stops recording keystrokes to a file
   @103[Operating System Shell]    - Shells to the Operating System
   @104[Operating System Shell Command]    - Shells to the OS with a command
   @42[Sport files]               - Open sport files (not avail 2100)
   @45[HIP files]                 - Open HIP files (2111&2150)

.180
Register Menu Option
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This submenu controls register related functions of the simulator.  Choices 
within this submenu are:

   @23[Computational]           - Displays computational registers
   @23[Alternate Computational] - Displays Alternate computational registers
   @21[DAG Computational]       - Displays DAG registers 
   @31[Program Control]         - Displays program control registers
   @35[Interrupt]               - Displays interrupt control registers
   @33[Status]                  - Displays Status registers
   @29[Control]                 - Displays Control registers
   @34[Flag]                    - Displays Flag registers
   @36[PX Register]             - Displays PX Register 
   @37[CE Register]             - Displays CE Register 
   @38[Sport 0  Register]       - Displays Sport 0  Register 
   @38[Sport 1  Register]       - Displays Sport 1  Register 
   @43[HIP Register]            - Displays HIP  Registers
   @46[CODEC Register]          - Displays CODEC/Powerdown  Registers
.181
Memory Menu Option
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This submenu controls register related functions of the simulator.  Choices
within this submenu are:

      @56[Data Memory Display]       - Displays Data Memory (DM)
         @114[Symbol Display (Alpha)] - Displays DM symbols alphabetically
         @114[Symbol Display (Num)]   - Displays DM symbols in numerical order
      @52[Program Memory Display]    - Displays Program Memory (PM)
         @109[Symbol Display (Alpha)] - Displays PM symbols alphabetically
         @109[Symbol Display (Num)]   - Displays PM symbols in numerical order
      @48[Boot Memory Display]       - Displays Boot Memory (BM)
         @111[Symbol Display (Alpha)] - Displays BM symbols alphabetically
         @111[Symbol Display (Num)]   - Displays BM symbols in numerical order
         @113[Delete Symbols]         - Deletes all symbols
      @165[Port Display]              - Displays port status
         @164[Open]                   - Opens a port
         @163[Close]                  - Closes a port
      @60[Dump Memory]               - Dumps memory to a file
      @61[Load Memory]               - Loads memory from a file
      @62[Fill Memory]               - Fills memory with a pattern
      @63[Go To Address]             - Changes window to a particular address
.182
Stacks Menu Option
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This submenu controls stack related functions of the simulator.  Choices within
this submenu are:

               @108[Loop Address] - Displays the loop address stack
               @107[Loop Counter] - Displays the loop counter stack
               @105[PC]           - Displays the PC stack
               @106[Status]       - Displays the status stack
.183
Command Menu Option
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This submenu controls the command line related functions of the simulator.  Choices within
this submenu are:

                  @76[Command  Line]   - Command line editor 
                  @84[Command  Output] - Command Output
.184
Execution Menu Option
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This submenu controls execution related functions of the simulator.  Choices
within this submenu are:

   @118[Run]                        - Runs a simulation
   @116[Step]                       - Executes a single step
   @117[Step 'n' Times]             - Executes 'n' single steps
   @170[Display Breakpoints]        - Displays all breakpoints
   @168[Set/Clear Breakpoint]       - Sets/Clears a breakpoint
   @169[Set/Clear Multi-Breakpoint] - Sets/Clears a multi-breakpoint
   @171[Clear All Breakpoints]      - Clears all breakpoints
.185
Display Menu Option
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This submenu controls display related functions of the simulator.  Choices
within this submenu are:

 @70[Color Attributes]     - Display/Modify the color attributes of the display
 @71[Floating Point Attr.] - Display/Modify the way floating point data is displayed
 @19[Video Mode]           - Display/Modify the video mode of the display
 @18[Toggle Window Format] - Toggles window display format
 @8[List Windows]         - List all open windows
 @7[Center Windows]       - Centers all open windows
 @6[Redraw Display]       - Redraws the display
.186
Misc Menu Option
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This submenu controls miscellaneous functions of the simulator.  Choices within
this submenu are:

              @68[Chip Reset]         - Simulates a chip reset signal
              @93[Defaults Menu]       - Defaults Menu
              @174[Interrupt Timing]   - Interrupt Timing
              @89[Expressions ]       - Display expressions
              @91[Break Expressions ] - Display break expressions
              @79[Trace ]             - Display Trace
              @85[Profile  ]          - Display Profile
              @20[About Simulator...] - Simulator Information
.187
Quit Menu Option
     @0[Return to Simulator]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @178[General Info]

This submenu controls functions related to exiting simulator.  Choices within
this submenu are:

                @2[Exit] - Exit simulator and update window file
                @3[Quit] - Exit simulator without updating window file
.End